From 868a44d9b5d428a96042c8c5707af6fded7c29c0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Minkovsky <dminkovsky@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 11:43:18 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Show an apply's catalog step from its row

The step an apply of a catalog release waits on (reading a release, or
fetching its cover, from a catalog) travelled to the screen on a fast
stream, though it changes a few times per apply. The apply now writes each
step to its own row in import_catalog_apply_step as the read starts and
deletes it as the read ends. A task deletes the row of an apply dropped
mid-read, and the library's open empties the table, since no apply
outlives the process.

The library's handle makes the apply with a new id, and the apply's live
query of its row is what the Mac's pick row and release editor read. The
stream, the host's constructor of the apply and BaeKit's step stream are
gone. Android reads no step.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
